4. TURKISH–ARABIC DICTIONARY ENHANCEMENT

Wara2ty has an important use case for students studying Turkish.

Improve the existing vocabulary feature into a more useful Turkish–Arabic academic dictionary experience.

Requirements:

- Display the original Turkish word.
- Display its Arabic meaning.
- Identify the word type when reliable.
- Show multiple meanings when available.
- Explain the meaning according to the lecture context.
- Provide a simple example when supported.
- Identify important suffixes or grammatical information when relevant.
- Allow students to save important vocabulary.
- Allow searching for a word inside the current lecture.

Dictionary data integration

Design the dictionary so that it can use a structured external dictionary dataset or an authorized dictionary API.

A possible open-data source is Turkish Wiktionary data extracted through Wiktextract (Kaikki).

Source:
https://kaikki.org/trwiktionary/rawdata.html

Do not assume this dataset contains complete Turkish–Arabic coverage.

Inspect its actual fields, language codes, translation availability, and licensing before integration.

Do not scrape proprietary dictionary applications or copy copyrighted dictionary databases without permission.

Use a dictionary provider/data adapter so the dictionary source can be replaced or expanded later.

When a reliable dictionary entry is unavailable, the AI may provide a contextual translation, but it must be clearly distinguished from a verified dictionary entry.

